# ELECTRIC FIRE / SMOKE ON GROUND (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist booklet, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05, page 16 (owner decisions 2026-10-23, 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28: the booklet is binding): the heading, every item, action and comment line as printed. The row marks are the numbers 1 to 5 as the booklet counts them. It is ONE list: the booklet has no branch for an engine that has stopped already, so the scenario has no variants and the engine runs at the start. Power lever Ground Idle (GI) is the lever position p0; Fuel valve OFF is the state off of the FUEL selector; the Doors row is graded on the door release lever (state open); the centred printed line Evacuate has no panel action and stays a comment line. All other text is own wording. The smoke source, the outcome threshold and hold time and the onset window are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: elec-fire-ground
title: ELEC FIRE GROUND
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: "Page 16, ELECTRIC FIRE / SMOKE ON GROUND"
  verified: "2026-10-28"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: parked
briefing:
  situation: "You are on the apron with the engine running when you smell burning plastic and smoke fills the cabin. No message is shown on the primary flight display. The smoke is getting thicker and its source seems to be electrical."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.power: p25
    lv.parking_brake: set
  quantities:
    airspeed_kt: 0
    smoke_density: 40
# ground_roll with the parking brake set: the aircraft stands, the PFD speed reads 0 knots (the brake holds it although the engine runs).
parameters:
  smoke_source: 1
  ground_roll: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: ELECTRIC FIRE / SMOKE ON GROUND
procedure[7]:
  - kind: group
    id: grp_elect_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 1
        text: Electric master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_power
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: power_idle
        severity: critical
        number: 2
        text: Power lever
        action: GROUND IDLE (GI)
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.power
          is: p0
  - kind: group
    id: grp_fuel_valve
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: fuel_valve_off
        severity: critical
        number: 3
        text: Fuel valve
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_valve
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_eng_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: engine_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: 4
        text: Engine master
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.engine_master
          is: off
  - kind: comment
    text: "After standstill and when engine stopped:"
  - kind: group
    id: grp_door
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: door_open
        severity: critical
        number: 5
        text: Doors
        action: OPEN
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: comment
    text: Evacuate
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the cabin stays full of smoke; the density and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: cabin_smoke_full
    text: Cabin full of smoke
    hold_s: 30
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: smoke_density
      op: gte
      value: 95
# The smoke of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the window is an instructor-review value.
# The smoke shows over the panel, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that it shows within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  quantities:
    airspeed_kt: 0
  cues[1]: cabin_smoke
